# Only repo metadata is ignored. Everything else deploys to every machine,
# including config that a given platform cannot use — an unread
# ~/.config/ghostty on the devserver costs nothing and keeps the two machines
# identical.
#
# This is safe because platform-specific behaviour is handled where it
# executes, not by withholding files:
#   - run_once_activate_key_remapping.sh and run_once_set_macos_defaults.sh
#     both exit 0 immediately when uname is not Darwin.
#   - run_once_configure_macos.sh, run_onchange_install-packages.sh, and
#     run_onchange_install-linux-packages.sh are template-gated on
#     .chezmoi.os and render to a bare shebang off their platform.
# Add a guard to the script rather than an entry here.
